{%- comment -%}
  The background-image layer for one skate-page section.

  Renders nothing when no image is set, which is what keeps the flat sections
  exactly as they were — no wrapper, no stacking context, no change.

  DECORATIVE, so `alt` is empty and the layer is aria-hidden. A background
  photograph that a screen reader announces is noise between the heading and the
  content; if a picture carries meaning here it belongs in the content, not
  behind it.

  EAGER, NOT LAZY, and this is the one place on the page where that is right. A
  lazily-loaded background paints after the text has already been read against
  the flat colour, which flashes. It is one image per section and it is the
  first thing visible in that section.

  Usage, as the first child of the .aj-grind wrapper:
    {% render 'aj-grind-bg', settings: section.settings %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if settings.bg_image != blank -%}
  <span class="aj-grind__bg" aria-hidden="true">
    <img
      src="{{ settings.bg_image | image_url: width: 2000 }}"
      srcset="{{ settings.bg_image | image_url: width: 750 }} 750w,
              {{ settings.bg_image | image_url: width: 1100 }} 1100w,
              {{ settings.bg_image | image_url: width: 1500 }} 1500w,
              {{ settings.bg_image | image_url: width: 2000 }} 2000w"
      sizes="100vw"
      alt=""
      width="{{ settings.bg_image.width }}"
      height="{{ settings.bg_image.height }}"
      loading="eager"
    >
  </span>
{%- endif -%}
